        "path": "_m/d/1/x/6/ancon-hill-wp/hero.jpg",
        "filename": "Plaque at the Top of Ancon Hill Commemorating Torrijos Carter Treaty.jpg",
        "caption": "Commemorative plaque marking the signing of the Torrijos–Carter Treaties on 7 September 1977 in Washington, D.C. The treaties were signed by Panamanian leader Omar Torrijos Herrera and United States President Jimmy Carter and established the gradual transfer of control of the Panama Canal to Panama, completed in 1999. The plaque lists the principal negotiators from Panama and the United States and references the role of the Organization of American States.",
        "alt": "Commemorative plaque marking the signing of the Torrijos–Carter Treaties on 7 September 1977 in Washington, D.C. The treaties were signed by Panamanian leader Omar Torrijos Herrera and United States President Jimmy Carter and established the gradual transfer of control of the Panama Canal to Panama, completed in 1999. The plaque lists the principal negotiators from Panama and the United States and references the role of the Organization of American States.",
