          "filename": "Folie Dingler (Ancon).jpg",
          "caption": "\"At the foot of Ancon Hill, facing the Balboa road, stood La Folie Dingler, the house built by M. Dingler, one of the chief engineers in the days of the First French Company. It was never occupied by him but was used by the Americans as a quarantine station ; afterwards demolished to make room for the Ancon hill quarry operations.\".",
